-- title:
--   Formally smooth centred subalgebra at a smooth pole-chart centre, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $q$ is a prime subject to `hq2 : q = 2`, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$.
--
--   **Arithmetic base data.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ belongs to `A.nonunits`; $\kappa_A$ denotes its residue field. $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A, M')$ — the $\kappa_A$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\kappa_A)$ generated by `jqModC` and `jqNModC`$(M')$ — and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. of those places $w$ which are rational (the structure map of $\kappa_A$ into the residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and for which $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q`. Here a place of $F$ over $K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, whose ring is a principal ideal ring; `ord` is the negative logarithm of the associated adic valuation and `evalAt` is evaluation of a unit of the valuation ring through the inverse of $K \to$ residue field.
--
--   Write $\mathcal F_{M'} = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(M')$ for the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change `laurentBaseChange` of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$, and $\mathcal F = \mathrm{fieldBar}(q,M')$ for the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H = \mathrm{levelH}(q,M')$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts $\mathcal F_{M'} \le \mathcal F$.
--
--   $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on $\mathcal F_{M'}$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\mathcal F_{M'}$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with orders of functions, meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ exactly in $A$ and inducing on constants the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero function becomes, after scaling by a constant, an integral function with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ lies in $\mathcal F_{M'}$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Further, $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ and $\pi \in A$, and $\zeta$ is an element of $\mathrm{Idx}(q)$, i.e. a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   **The two families of valuation rings.** $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}} : \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q) \to$ valuation subrings of $\mathcal F$ (written `OIg`, indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21)) and $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}} : W \to$ valuation subrings of $\mathcal F$ (written `OSS`). Four hypotheses govern $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$: `hIg_inf` identifies $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$, the ring at the line $\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q = [1:0]$, as the set of $f \in \mathcal F$ admitting Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ is nonzero and $f$ times the image of $y$ equals the image of $x$; `hIg` provides, for every $\ell$, a matrix $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{redQ}(q)(\gamma)\cdot\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q = \ell$ and $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along the automorphism $\mathrm{levelAutBar}(q,M',\zeta,\gamma)$ of $\mathcal F$; `hIg_inj` that $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; `hIg_perm` that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}(q,M',\zeta',\gamma)$ permutes the family $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   Four hypotheses govern $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}$. `hSS_A`: for every $s$ and every $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$, the image of $x$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ if and only if $x \in A$. `hSS_over`: for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that $f$ has non-negative order at every place of $\mathcal F_{M'}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the element $\hat\jmath \in \mathcal F_{M'}$ obtained from the $q$-expansion `jq` by `coeffEmb` has non-negative order, and such that the residue $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ lies in the valuation ring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(f))$ the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal. `hSS_fix`: each $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ is its own pullback along every $\mathrm{levelAutBar}(q,M',\zeta',\gamma)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$. `hSS_tr`: for each $s$ there is $t \in \mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ such that for every $a \in A$ the element $t$ minus the image of $a$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   **Descent data.** $K_0$ is a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over it and $\pi \in K_0$; $A_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring (a domain) with an injective local ring homomorphism $\iota : A_0 \to A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A \cap K_0$ (`hιK₀`), such that the residue map of $A$ composed with $\iota$ is surjective (`hres`); $\varpi_0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_0$ and $\iota(\varpi_0) = \pi$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   $F_0$ is a subfield of $\mathcal F$ characterised by `hF₀` as the set of those $f$ all of whose Laurent coefficients lie in $K_0$; by `hjF₀` the image of $\hat\jmath$ in $\mathcal F$ lies in $F_0$, and this element of $F_0$, again written $\hat\jmath$, is assumed nonzero. $F_0$ carries an $A_0$-algebra structure which by `hj₀` is the one induced by $\iota$ followed by $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathcal F$.
--
--   **The refinement and its centre on the pole chart.** Write $C = \mathrm{chartAlgInf}(A_0,F_0,\hat\jmath)$ for the pole chart, that is, the $A_0$-subalgebra of $F_0$ of elements integral over $A_0[\hat\jmath^{-1}]$. $V$ is a valuation subring of $F_0$ with: `hV`, the image in $\mathcal F$ of every element of $V$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$; `hVlt`, some element of $F_0$ has image in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ but does not lie in $V$, so the containment is strict; `hCV`, $C \subseteq V$. The ideal $\mathfrak n$ of $C$ is maximal (`h𝔫max`) and is the centre of $V$ on $C$: $g \in \mathfrak n$ if and only if $g$ lies in `V.nonunits` (`h𝔫`).
--
--   `hnotSS` expresses that $\mathfrak n$ is not a supersingular centre, in the disjunctive sense: for every $s \in W$, either some $g \in C$ has image in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ lying in its maximal ideal while $g \notin \mathfrak n$, or some $g \in C$ has image outside $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$.
--
--   **Igusa component primes and generic fibre on the chart.** $\mathfrak q : \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q) \to$ ideals of $C$ satisfies: `hLOC`, for every $\ell$ and $x \in F_0$, the image of $x$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ if and only if $x = b/c$ with $b,c \in C$ and $c \notin \mathfrak q(\ell)$; `hMIN`, each $\mathfrak q(\ell)$ is a minimal prime over the ideal of $C$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$; `hINJ`, $\mathfrak q$ is injective; `hSURJ`, every minimal prime over that ideal is of the form $\mathfrak q(\ell)$. `hGENFIB` requires that every nonzero prime $\mathfrak p$ of $C$ not containing the image of $\varpi_0$ gives a valuation subring $V_1$ of $F_0$ with $f \in V_1$ if and only if $f = b/c$ for some $b,c \in C$ with $c \notin \mathfrak p$.
--
--   **Smoothness.** $U$ is an open subscheme of the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}(A_0,F_0,\hat\jmath)$, the pushout of the two maps from the middle chart to the finite and infinite charts; `hxU` places the image under $\iota_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ of the point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ given by $\mathfrak n$ in $U$, and `hU` asserts that the immersion $U.\iota$ followed by the structure morphism $\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A_0$ is smooth.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist an $A_0$-subalgebra $B$ of $F_0$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $B$ such that all of the following hold.
--
--   1. $B$ is a finitely generated $A_0$-algebra (`B.FG`).
--
--   2. $B$ is integrally closed in $F_0$: every $x \in F_0$ integral over $B$ lies in $B$.
--
--   3. $F_0$ is the field of fractions of $B$: every $x \in F_0$ satisfies $x\,c = b$ for some $b, c \in B$ with $c \neq 0$.
--
--   4. Every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ containing the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ and not maximal is a minimal prime over that image ideal.
--
--   5. For every nonzero prime $\mathfrak p$ of $B$ not containing the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$, there is a valuation subring $V_1$ of $F_0$ with $f \in V_1$ if and only if $f = b/c$ for some $b,c \in B$ with $c \notin \mathfrak p$.
--
--   6. For $\ell' \in \mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, if the image in $\mathcal F$ of every element of $B$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell')$, then $\ell' = \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$.
--
--   7. For no $s \in W$ does the image in $\mathcal F$ of every element of $B$ lie in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$.
--
--   8. There is a prime ideal $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ such that for all $x \in F_0$ the image of $x$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ if and only if $x\,c = b$ for some $b,c \in B$ with $c \notin \mathfrak q$.
--
--   9. Every minimal prime $\mathfrak q$ over the image in $B$ of the maximal ideal of $A_0$ has the same property: for all $x \in F_0$, the image of $x$ lies in $\mathcal O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ if and only if $x\,c = b$ with $b,c \in B$, $c \notin \mathfrak q$.
--
--   10. $B \subseteq V$, and $\mathfrak m$ is the centre of $V$ on $B$: $b \in \mathfrak m$ if and only if $b \in V.\mathrm{nonunits}$.
--
--   11. Either $\hat\jmath \in B$ or $\hat\jmath^{-1} \in B$.
--
--   12. The structure homomorphism from $A_0$ to the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak m$ is formally smooth.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case of the pole-chart step in the Igusa-chart dichotomy for the full-level semistable covering: starting from a proper refinement $V$ of the Igusa ring at the line at infinity whose centre on the chart $A_0[\hat\jmath^{-1}]^{\mathrm{int}}$ is a smooth point of the two-chart integral model over $A_0$ and is not a supersingular centre, it produces a finitely generated, integrally closed $A_0$-subalgebra of $F_0$ carrying the full package of localisation, fibre and separation properties, with formally smooth localisation at the centre of $V$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_centred_formallySmooth_or_exists_forall_mem_nonunits_of_le_gaussRing_descent_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_subalgebra_centred_formallySmooth_or_exists_forall_mem_nonunits_of_le_gaussRing_descent_of_eq_two), which turns this package into the dichotomy alternative.
